      "originalText": "n is a transitive child of the redone grave x (via the branch-local grave g) — the redo never saw it.\nSame 2b lesson one level up: a grave’s children — including ones that arrived through branch-local\ngraves — must be placed by ONE computation that sees ALL of them.",
