      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783755609633,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "YES here — and keeping Q means frozen = canonical (no frames).\nBut keep must be CONDITIONAL:\n· existing sibling: our first bug! del a with c·3 under it\n  leapfrogs b·2 if c keeps 3\n· concurrent: keep n·7 under g·3, concurrent p·5 →\n  oracle p n, keep gives n p ✗.  Works here only because\n  no integer fits in (3,4).\n⇒ keep iff nothing can land between grave rank and kept Q;\n   else clip-bake into (⌈hi⌉−1, hi).   → testing as variant K",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 9.600000000000001,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "YES here — and keeping Q means frozen = canonical (no frames).\nBut keep must be CONDITIONAL:\n· existing sibling: our first bug! del a with c·3 under it\n  leapfrogs b·2 if c keeps 3\n· concurrent: keep n·7 under g·3, concurrent p·5 →\n  oracle p n, keep gives n p ✗.  Works here only because\n  no integer fits in (3,4).\n⇒ keep iff nothing can land between grave rank and kept Q;\n   else clip-bake into (⌈hi⌉−1, hi).   → testing as variant K",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b4k",
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "kc-ans-fresh",
      "x": 998.7751096727152,
      "y": 4486.749115446221,
      "width": 261.3835754394531,
      "height": 120,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4a63e0",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 9503,
      "version": 43,
      "versionNonce": 1358772790,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783755615100,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "YES — A performed the deletes, so A’s copy\nof c is FRESH (parent=root survives);\nL’s copy is stale (parent=x, removed).\nRule: take the branch copy whose stored\nparent is NOT being removed; redo only\nwhen no branch has one (the 2001←4 case).\nFixes CX-F with no redo; CX-P still needs\nthe clip.   → testing as variant F (+clip)",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "baseline": 9.600000000000001,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "YES — A performed the deletes, so A’s copy\nof c is FRESH (parent=root survives);\nL’s copy is stale (parent=x, removed).\nRule: take the branch copy whose stored\nparent is NOT being removed; redo only\nwhen no branch has one (the 2001←4 case).\nFixes CX-F with no redo; CX-P still needs\nthe clip.   → testing as variant F (+clip)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b4l",
      "autoResize": true
    }
